cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:17:Both-zero terminal W/L/D gives no ranking signal between these policies. Econ.2 is a capped death-potential difference, not a penalty for arbitrary spending or a bank-profit target. The current-policy diagnostic also accumulates8193 ineffective unit commands; economic production chains remain unlearned. Prior cookbook search found no qualified v3 BC implementation; v2's public replay loader provides observation/action alignment and shared-field semantics, not its model, collector or training code.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:23:- `ops/bc-bootstrap-2026-09-29/select_replays.py`, `prepare.py`: read-only source volume4llk4uaf20, source days09-21..27, seeded32 training and4 validation episodes/day.252 episodes are split by identity, with duplicate episode IDs rejected. Hash each source payload and prepared shard. Pair observation[t] with action[t+1], fill seat1 schema-shared fields, and preserve own-private encoding. Missing units become explicit NONE; never truncate market orders or quantities. Replay JSON is processed once offline; resident GPU arrays feed BC minibatches.
